Gave every driver config field an explicit position. A driver declares its settings in the order an operator should meet them — issuer before the client credentials, the scope before the two behavioural switches — but a schema travels as a JSON object and plone.restapi serialises those with `sort_keys=True`, so what reached the control panel was alphabetical whatever the driver wrote. `auto_link_by_email` came first, and the issuer that decides what the rest of the form even means came fourth.

Each descriptor now carries an `order`, spaced by ten so a driver can slot a field between two inherited ones without renumbering anything, and the form sorts on that rather than on the key. Two fields claiming the same position is a test failure rather than a silent fall back to alphabetical, since a tie is exactly the bug this replaced hiding in one driver instead of all of them. @ericof
